%%%
Weak convergence in a real normed space gives convergence against each continuous functional:

$$`
x_\alpha\rightharpoonup x
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\ell(x_\alpha)\longrightarrow\ell(x)
\qquad(\ell\in H^*).
`
:::

:::proof "analysis.weak_compactness.evaluation"
The weak topology on $`H` is the initial topology generated by all continuous
linear functionals $`\ell:H\to\mathbb R`. Therefore each evaluation map is
continuous by construction. Applying that continuity to
$`x_\alpha\rightharpoonup x` gives
$`\ell(x_\alpha)\to\ell(x)` for every $`\ell\in H^*`.
:::

Reflexivity and Banach–Alaoglu give the compactness half of the direct
method: a norm bound on a minimizing sequence, together with weak closedness
of the sublevel set it lives in, is enough to produce a weak cluster point.

:::theorem "analysis.weak_compactness.bounded_closed" (parent := "methods.direct_method") (lean := "PDE.Analysis.WeakCompactness.isCompact_of_isClosed_of_isBounded") (uses := "analysis.weak_compactness.hilbert_reflexive")
%%%
source := {
  document := "evans-pde"
  spans := #[{
